      "body": "Fix HY-V4 checkpoint-backed learnable sink loading in NVIDIA target/MTP and AMD target models. The AMD target path was omitted from the original series and is included here.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe runtime parameter already has local TP shape. `load_weights` takes the rank slice once and passes it to the parameter's current `weight_loader`; no padded helper or second sharding loader is needed. The AMD and NVIDIA target paths preserve their TP slicing, load the local shard through the current `weight_loader`, and use the same shared `loaded_params` path.\r\r\n\r\r\n## Validation\r\r\n\r\r\n- This PR changes only three HY-V4 files. `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, and `git diff --check` pass.\r\r\n- Static validation on the integrated final tree: `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `git diff --check`, and test tethering pass. The source audit passes 28 tests. The new runtime tests have not been executed, as requested.\r\r\n\r\r\n## AI assistance\r\r\n\r\r\nAI assistance was used.\r\r\n",
